# Taskmark file conventions

When creating or editing files under `taskmark/`:

- Keep required YAML frontmatter including `size` (null on epics), `points`, `estimate_minutes`, `actual_minutes`, `session_cap_minutes`, sources/basis fields, and standard id/status/parent fields. Epic points = sum of stories; story points = sum of tasks when children exist.
- Do **not** hand-set `status` except via `blocked` / `cancelled`; after edits run sync-status.
- **Never** hand-set `effort_minutes` or `actual_minutes`. Run `scripts/recompute-actuals.py` (from sync-status / complete-work).
- **Never** invent ≤2 minute closed Work log sessions for delivered work. Close real open sessions with **now** UTC.
- **Never** set `effort_minutes` from calendar span. Effort = billable work-log sessions only (idle auto-cap: next-day 12:00 UTC; session_cap_minutes default 480). Commit-span recovery feeds effort only. `actual_minutes` is wall-clock `started_at`→`completed_at` written by the script.
- Idle: auto-close open sessions at next-day 12:00 UTC when syncing / starting / completing work.
- **Work log** and **Commits** on every item; **Prompt & feedback** on stories/tasks/bugs.
- Refresh `INDEX.md` (Points / Est / Actual) and `VELOCITY.md` via recompute / sync-status; calibrate estimates with `--calibrate` when finishing work.
- Follow `taskmark-conventions` skill templates.
